Subject: modadmin: a locked module's unload delay reads never

modstat reports a module that does not declare unload=allowed as locked
(patch 0016), and the core never unloads a locked one, so the delay it
carries (the default 60 s) is never used.  -q, -Q and -S printed it all
the same: "Unload Delay: 60 seconds" beside "Flags: locked".  A locked
module's line now reads "never (locked)" (amix-dlm N235c).

--- a/modadmin.c
+++ b/modadmin.c
@@ -306,7 +306,10 @@
 	printf("Module Size:\t\t%u\n", st->ms_size);
 	printf("Base Address:\t\t0x%lx\n", (unsigned long)st->ms_base);
 	printf("Module Revision:\t%d\n", st->ms_rev);
-	printf("Unload Delay:\t\t%ld seconds\n", (long)st->ms_unload_delay);
+	if (st->ms_flags & MS_LOCKED)	/* pinned (unload=never) or held */
+		printf("Unload Delay:\t\tnever (locked)\n");
+	else
+		printf("Unload Delay:\t\t%ld seconds\n", (long)st->ms_unload_delay);
 	printf("Reference Count:\t%d\n", st->ms_refcnt);
 	printf("Dependent Count:\t%d\n", st->ms_depcnt);
 	printf("Flags:\t\t\t%s%s%s\n", st->ms_flags & MS_DEMAND ? "demand " : "",
